  "=segments": [
    {
      "index": 0,
      "text": "You can keep these manifests as Markdown. No tooling required. Later, they’re easy to convert to ZONJ/JSON.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 1,
      "text": "Book 5 overview: what “structure and perimeter walls” actually build",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "text": "This book is the pivot where “the Nameless One” becomes a named protagonist, binds to larger forces, and the rebellion stops being “survive” and becomes “offensive operations.”",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "text": "The Nameless One’s defiance becomes contagious, watched by Anunnaki decision-makers who choose to keep the “flaw” instead of recycling it.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "text": "chapter_24_the_first_spark",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 5,
      "text": "A Pleiadian arrival and slave-market selection scene clarifies the wider galaxy’s complicity, and the Nameless One pockets a dropped crystal device.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 6,
      "text": "chapter_24_the_first_spark",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 7,
      "text": "By the end, “Ragnarok” is no longer a label applied to him, but an identity he claims publicly, triggering a formal galactic threat record and maximum bounty.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 8,
      "text": "chapter_28_ragnarok",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 9,
      "text": "Name map (the “few names” you called out)",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 10,
      "text": "Nehoreti / Nehereti / Nephoretti",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 11,
      "text": "In these chapters, the text uses “Nehereti” as the beings tied to Tiamat’s remnants and Zaron’s hiding/guarding network.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 12,
      "text": "chapter_26_dragonmail",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 13,
      "text": "Your chosen canon spelling is: Nephoretti.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 14,
      "text": "Manifest rule: treat Nehoreti / Nehereti / Neforreti / etc as aliases, and normalize all to Nephoretti in the glossary + manifests.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 15,
      "text": "Solantri",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 16,
      "text": "Not present in Books 1–5 content you provided. Based on your note: “not on earth” yet. So for now it stays a glossary stub: “off-world group/civilization encountered later.”",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 17,
      "text": "Gravitons",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 18,
      "text": "Not present in Books 1–5 content you provided. Based on your note: “deep lore / end game.” So for now: glossary stub, no invented details.",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 19,
      "text": "BOOK 5 MANIFEST PACK (Chapters 24–28)",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 20,
      "text": "Chapter 24: The First Spark",
      "type": "narration"
    },
    {
      "index": 21,
      "text": "Logline\nA disposable slave commits a first impossible act of defiance, becomes visible to both fellow prisoners and the Anunnaki, and is dragged into a larger galactic economy when Pleiadians arrive for procurement.",
      "type": "narration"
